BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Golden Anniversary Gala and Off the Wall Art Lottery
DTSTART:20261107T170000
DTEND:20261107T210000
DTSTAMP:20261107T165455Z
UID:cc39fbbdd9ea59e44ecdbc04d5b6b2@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate River Gallery School's 50th anniversary at our bigge
 st fundraiser of the year! Enjoy an evening of dinner\, birthday cake\, an
 d Off the Wall—our beloved art lottery where everyone wins. With a $200 
 Participant Ticket\, you'll receive one original work of art donated by lo
 cal and regional artists. Throughout the evening\, lottery numbers are dra
 wn one at a time. When your number is called\, you'll choose your favorite
  available piece from the wall. Every participant goes home with artwork. 
 Can't attend in person? You can participate remotely by sending us a ranke
 d list of your favorite pieces. When your number is drawn\, we'll reserve 
 the highest-ranked artwork still available and arrange pickup or shipping.
  Artwork may be previewed online before the event or in person throughout 
 October at Gallery 34\, River Gallery School\, 34 Main Street\, Brattlebor
 o. Participant Ticket: $200 (includes one original artwork) Non-Participan
 t Ticket: $35 (join the celebration without participating in the art lotte
 ry) Retreat Farm\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Vermont Public is independent\, community-supported media\, servi
 ng Vermont with trusted\, relevant and essential information. We share sto
 ries that bring people together\, from every corner of our region.\, © 20
 26 Vermont Public | 365 Troy Ave. Colchester\, VT 05446
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/golden-ann
 iversary-gala-and-off-the-wall-art-lottery-27-07-2026-12-29-39
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Growing What Comes Next
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261107
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261108
DTSTAMP:20261107T165455Z
UID:0953884e54403adaf3c0863fedafb0@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:A conversation with Joe Bossen and Racheal Ouellette from Clou
 d Water Farm\, Muddy Boots CSA\, and Vermont Bean Crafters. All are welcom
 e to join us for a conversation with Joe Bossen and Racheal Ouellette as t
 hey share the vision\, creativity\, and hard work behind their interconnec
 ted ventures and what’s next for farming and food systems in Vermont. Th
 rough photographs\, stories\, and examples of their work\, they’ll explo
 re exciting new projects\, including a multifaceted community barn\, clima
 te-resilient farming\, seed saving\, willow growing and weaving\, support 
 for emerging farms\, and expanding access to locally produced food. They w
 ould love to answer your questions and ideas about how farming can connect
  food\, ecology\, entrepreneurship\, and community to shape a more resilie
 nt future.\n\nSources: Vermont.com\, Vermont Public
LOCATION:Mad River Valley Arts\, 5031 Main Street\, Unit 2
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/growing-wh
 at-comes-next-15-10-2026-21-44-52
END:VEVENT
